{"id":"word:hebrew:H1835","type":"word","title":"דָּן","subtitle":"H1835 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Dan , one of the sons of Jacob; also the tribe descended from him, and its territory; likewise a place in Palestine colonized by them","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to דָּן (H1835) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 70 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"דָּן (Dân) means Dan , one of the sons of Jacob; also the tribe descended from him, and its territory; likewise a place in Palestine colonized by them First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"דָּן","transliteration":"Dân","pronunciation":"dawn","strong":"H1835","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1835","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["דָ֔ן","דָ֖ן","דָּ֔ן","דָּ֖ן","דָּֽן"],"morphs":[["HNp",55],["HR/Np",12],["HC/R/Np",1],["HC/Np",1],["HR/R/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Dan , one of the sons of Jacob; also the tribe descended from him, and its territory; likewise a place in Palestine colonized by them","usage":"Daniel","full":"H1835. Dan דָּן proper name, masculine ( judge ) — 1 son of Jacob and Bilhah Gen 30:6 ; 35:25 ; Exod 1:4 ; Josh 19:47 ; Judg 18:29 ; 1Chr 2:2 . 2 the tribe of Dan , דָן מַטֵּה Exod 31:6 ; 35:34 ; 38:23 ; Lev 24:11 ; Num 1:39 ; 13:12 ; Josh 21:5 , 23 (all P); דָן בְּנֵי Gen 46:23 ; Num 1:38 ; 2:25 ; 7:66 ; 10:25 ; 26:42 ; 34:22 ; Josh 19:40 , 47 (twice in verse); 19:48 (all P) Judg 1:34 ; 18:2 , 16 , 22 , 23 , 25 , 26 , 30 ; דָן מַחֲנֵה Num 2:25 , 31 (P) — on Judg 13:25 ; 18:12 see מַחֲנֶה ; דָּן מִשְׁמְּחֹת Num 26:42 (P); דָּן alone in poetry Gen 49:16-17 , Deut 33:22 (twice in verse); Judg 5:17 , elsewhere Num 1:12 (P) Deut 27:13 ; 1Chr 27:22 ; 2Chr 2:13 ; Ezek 48:1-2 , 32 . 3 a city on northern frontier of Israel at one of the sources of the Jordan , originally לַיִשׁ Judg 18:29 (compare 18:7 ); = לֶשֶׁם Josh 19:47 ; captured by a colony of Danites; named Dan, and made a sacred place with rites of worship that lasted until the exile ( Judg 18:30 ); = Tell el Kâdî , Rob BR iii. 351, 358 Bd Pa1 265 . This place is frequently referred to: Gen 14:14 ; Deut 34:1 ; 1Kin 12:29-30 , 15:20 ; 2Kin 10:29 ; 2Chr 16:4 ; Jer 4:15 ; 8:16 ; Amos 8:14 ; read also וּבְדָן for וְכֵן 2Sam 20:18 ᵐ5 Ew We compare Dr; and see the phrase שֶׁבַע וְעַדבְּֿאֵר מִדָּן Judg 20:1 ; 1Sam 3:20 ; 2Sam 3:10 ; 17:11 ; 24:2 , 15 ; 1Kin 5:5 ; given by Chronicles וְעַדדָּֿן שֶׁבַע מִבְּאֵר 1Chr 21:2 ; 2Chr 30:5 . ( Ezek 27:19 see ודן .) Note. — יַעַן דָּ֫נָה 2Sam 24:6 . As no such place is known, the text is usually regarded as corrupt, and, ᵐ5 being uncertain, is variously changed: (1) יַעַר דָּ֫נָה to Dan in the wood , Thes after ᵑ9 silvestria. (2) ( וַיָּסֹבּוּ ) וְעִיּוֺן דָּ֫נָה to Dan and Ijon Klo (compare 1Kin 15:20 ). (3) ( סָֽבֲבוּ ) וּמִדָּן דָּן We Dr compare ᵐ5 .","rootNote":"from 1777 ; judge ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 2 2","keyReferences":["1Chr 2 2","1Chr 21 2","1Chr 27 22","1Kgs 5 5","1Kgs 12 29","1Kgs 12 30","1Kgs 15 20","1Sam 3 20"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":70,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 2 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָּ֚ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָּ֑ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 27 22","book":"1Chr","chapter":27,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/דָ֕ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Np"},{"reference":"1Kgs 5 5","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִ/דָּ֖ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Np"},{"reference":"1Kgs 12 29","book":"1Kgs","chapter":12,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/דָֽן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Np"},{"reference":"1Kgs 12 30"